  "explanation": {
    "short": "A silent ห in front of ม น ง ย ล ว is not said: it only turns the low-class letter into a high-class one. So หมา is just \"maa\", but it rises like ขา, and ไหม is \"mai\" with a rising tone.",
    "more": "The silent ห is how Thai spells the same smooth sounds in a high tone: compare มา (come, mid) with หมา (dog, rising). The tone mark after it follows the high class too: ใหม่ is low, like ข่าว. The letter อ does the same job for just four words: อยู่, อยาก, อย่า and อย่าง. It is silent and gives ย the mid class, so อยู่ (stay) and อยาก (want) are low."
  },
